ctrolytes", "Granulomatous disease (e.g., sarcoidosis): Could explain hypercalcemia but lacks typical respiratory symptoms"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Recreational/Over-the-Counter Medication Use", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.17857142857142858, "posterior": 0.23668639053254437, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Antacid overuse is a possible cause of hypercalcemia but does not typically elevate ALP significantly."], "evidence_against": ["Elevated ALP is inconsistent with hypercalcemia from antacid overuse, which typically does not affect ALP."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Endocrine Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.26785714285714285, "posterior": 0.09861932938856015, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Normal renal function and lack of polyuria/polydipsia make endocrine causes like hyperparathyroidism less likely."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Malignancy with Hypercalcemia and Elevated ALP", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.6153846153846153, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The combination of hypercalcemia, elevated ALP, and constitutional symptoms with weight loss is classically associated with malignancy."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Granulomatous Disease", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.016, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The combination of hypercalcemia, elevated ALP, and constitutional symptoms with weight loss is classically associated with malignancy."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Other Systemic Illness", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.033, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3.1": {"id": "B3.1", "label": "Solid Tumor with Bone Metastases (e.g., Breast, Lung, Prostate)", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2735042735042735, "posterior": 0.2735042735042735, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3.2": {"id": "B3.2", "label": "Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia and Lytic Lesions", "parent": "B3", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2051282051282051, "posterior": 0.2051282051282051, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "fam